Hi everyone, I've been out of the geomorph scene for a while and I'm trying to get myself reoriented with all of the changes that have been made in the past few years.

Is there now any automated way to measure and test for pairwise convergence and divergence between several groups in allometric trajectories? Like Table 3 in Piras et al. 2010, or Djuv and Dadult in Adams and Nistri 2010.

Unless I'm missing something it doesn't look like advanced.procD.lm(), procD.lm(), or procD.allometry() provide this specific output. And if I'm remembering correctly trajectory.analysis() is not appropriate for this type of analysis?

I've tried to do it pair by pair manually, but with so many pairs it's a bit daunting.
I've attached the code I've used if anyone wants to take a look, especially for the permutation procedure. I think that I correctly parsed out the methods described in those two papers, but I'm not entirely sure.

If anyone has any suggestions I'd appreciate it.

Thank you!

