Yes, I assume no one would really do a PCA for two specimens in reality, neither do I. I did test it with 4 specimens and the PCA works well. Just like you said, with two specimens, there is only one PC axis and there is no point of doing a PCA, that's probably why I had that error. I just recalled that I did a PCA for only two specimens with the Morphologika software. That's why I did this unreal test.

I could not find your update package on Github via the gh_install_packages ("geomorph") function and gh_list_pacakges(username="collyer") from the "githubinstall" package. I probably don't look for it in the right way, but I think it should be good as you said! Is it possible to let me know how to look for your update at github?

Best regards,
Charles

