Burak,

You have interaction term Site * Gender, so your model for test of homogeneity of slopes would be:

procD.allometry(Shape ~ CS, ~ Site * Gender, ...).

For pairwise slope comparisons it depends on your research question, but considering Help documentation I think your model should be:

advanced.procD.lm(Shape ~ CS + Site * Gender,
                                            ~ CS * Site * Gender,
                                               groups = ~ Site * Gender, slope = ~CS, ...)

Best,
Milena

2018-06-22 1:57 GMT+02:00 <bkara...@gmail.com>:
> Another thing is while the tests above are for learning purposes, in reality there is another factor, gender.  Shape and size both differ by gender and I have an unbalanced design. Even if the difference in shape between populations is significant I can't be sure because of the effect of gender. How can I account for both gender and size effects when comparing shape differences between populations? I can't leave out samples as I don't have enough samples in some populations (four times the number of landmarks).
